{
  "id": "T-1447",
  "created_at": 1790873172.0906172,
  "parent": "T-1403",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: bus.update may change depends_on of a not-yet-dispatched task (event recorded); create_task resolves plan-label refs in depends_on via constraints.plan_label",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, plan label E8. Evidence: 198 orchestrator tasks were re-filed only to change\ndepends_on (analysis-2026-10-01 finding 4); luna T-0240 wired 20 depends_on one id too low because the Planner\npredicted ids before creating them (plan.md backlog 2026-09-24).\n\nFacts (main 355583c):\n- orchestrator/bus.py:132-143 update() raises PermissionError for spec, acceptance, scope, complexity and\n  depends_on.\n- bus.py:101-129 create_task() validates each depends_on entry with get(dep) (KeyError -> ValueError 'depends_on\n  references unknown task'), refuses self-reference, drops a fix round's own fix_round_for parent and records a\n  'depends_on_normalized' event (_event at 84-85).\n- bus.read() lists tasks (197); constraints.plan_label is set by the Planner's filing script (T-1403 children carry\n  A1..A8, A1v2, A6v2, E1, E2).\n- orchestrator/bus_mcp.py:9-14 bus_create_task passes depends_on straight to bus.create_task.\n\nChange:\n1. update(): depends_on is allowed only when the current task is status 'queued' and has no\n   pipeline.dispatched_at. Validate inside the existing lock: list of str; every id exists; not the task itself; not\n   its constraints.fix_round_for; no cycle (walk depends_on of the new deps transitively; reaching tid is a cycle).\n   Record _event(tid, 'depends_on_changed', {'from': old, 'to': new}) besides the normal update event. All other\n   immutable fields stay refused.\n2. create_task(): before validation, map each depends_on entry that is not an existing task id: candidates = tasks\n   with constraints.plan_label == entry, parent == the new task's parent, status != 'superseded'. Exactly one ->\n   its id; none -> ValueError 'depends_on references unknown task or plan label: X'; several -> ValueError naming\n   them. Record _event(new id, 'depends_on_resolved', {label: id, ...}) when any label was resolved. Existing ids\n   keep working; the fix_round_for normalization runs after resolution.\n3. bus_mcp.py: bus_create_task docstring says depends_on accepts task ids or plan labels of siblings.\n4. Update the update() docstring.\n\nTests that assert the old behaviour (SPEC RULE; update to the new contract):\n- tests/test_bus.py::test_depends_on (~358-368) asserts bus.update(b, depends_on=[]) raises PermissionError while b\n  is queued and undispatched; under the new contract that call succeeds. Change it to set pipeline.dispatched_at\n  first (or status running) and keep the PermissionError assertion.\n- tests/test_bus.py::test_lifecycle_and_rules (~265-280) asserts PermissionError for scope: unchanged.\n- tests/test_bus.py::test_fix_round_drops_own_parent_from_depends_on and test_non_fix_round_depends_on_unchanged\n  (~370-395) must pass unchanged.\n\nOut of scope: daemon.py, a new MCP update tool.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1438"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_update_depends_on_before_dispatch_records_event: passes: bus.update(tid, depends_on=[...]) on a queued task with no pipeline.dispatched_at replaces depends_on, appends a 'depends_on_changed' event with from/to, and rejects unknown ids, self-reference, a cycle and the task's fix_round_for parent (ValueError); after pipeline.dispatched_at is set, or once status is not queued, it raises PermissionError as before",
    "tests/test_bus.py::test_create_task_resolves_plan_label_depends_on: passes: create_task(..., parent=G, depends_on=['B1']) stores the id of the one non-superseded child of G whose constraints.plan_label is 'B1' and records a 'depends_on_resolved' event; an unknown label or two live matches raise ValueError",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/bus.py",
    "orchestrator/bus_mcp.py",
    "tests/test_bus.py"
  ],
