  "result": {
    "summary": "The diff matches the spec and both acceptance tests are present. The gate was green on its first attempt, but I did not rerun the tests. create_task resolves plan labels among non-superseded siblings with the same parent. It raises ValueError for an unknown label or several matches, and records depends_on_resolved. Resolution runs before the fix_round_for normalization. update() allows depends_on only on a queued task with no pipeline.dispatched_at. All checks run inside the lock: type, existence, self-reference, fix_round_for parent and cycle. It records depends_on_changed with from and to. The other immutable fields still raise PermissionError. The old test_depends_on assertion was updated as the spec directs. The two nits are low risk and need no change.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/bus.py",
        "line": 168,
        "issue": "The cycle walk calls get(current) on transitive deps. If an existing task has a dangling depends_on id, update() raises a bare KeyError instead of ValueError. Also `t.get(\"pipeline\", {})` would raise AttributeError if a task stored pipeline=None. Both are unlikely, since create_task validates deps and pipeline is only set by the daemon.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/bus.py",
        "line": 118,
        "issue": "When parent is None, labels resolve against other parentless tasks that have the same plan_label. This follows the spec literally, but it could match unrelated root tasks. No change needed.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
